#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""artifact -- create, inspect and drive artifacts from an agent session.

Artifacts live in ~/reports/ and are served at https://dsh.example.com/report/<name>.
Everything you create here is attributed to your chat ($DSH_SESSION_ID), so it
shows up under "This chat" in the Artifacts sidebar tab.

CREATE
  artifact new <name> [--type T] [--title "..."]   scaffold and print path + URL
        T = report (default) | dashboard | plan | comparison | brief | interactive  -> <name>.md
            page   -> <name>.html (single self-contained page, bridge-ready)
            react  -> <name>/index.html + <name>/app.jsx (React 18 + Tailwind + JSX, no build)
            app    -> <name>/index.html + <name>/app.js (vanilla / preact-htm)
            motion -> <name>.html (player) + <name>.motion/index.html (HyperFrames composition)
                      [--size landscape|portrait|square|720p|WxH] [--duration 12]
  artifact url <name>                print the URL (md -> its rendered .html)
  artifact render <x.md>             write the .html next to the .md (optional: it renders on the fly)

INSPECT / UNDO
  artifact list [--all] [-n 20]      this chat's artifacts (or all)
  artifact show <name>               url, source file, versions, storage, public state
  artifact versions <name>           automatic snapshots (every change is kept, 40 per file)
  artifact diff <name> [A] [B]       unified diff between snapshots (default: last change)
  artifact restore <name> <v>        put a snapshot back

TWO-WAY
  artifact inbox [--clear]           what artifacts sent back silently (dsh.context, forms in
                                     context mode, runtime errors). Read it when the user says
                                     "I filled it in" / "look at the artifact".
  artifact state <name> [key]        read the artifact's persistent storage (dsh.storage)
  artifact state-set <name> <key> <json>   push data INTO a live artifact without rewriting
                                     it (the page reads it with dsh.storage.get / .watch)
  artifact public <name> on|off      public no-login link /report-public/<name>

MEDIA (files land in ~/reports/media/, embed with ![](media/x.png) or <img src>)
  artifact media image "<prompt>" [--provider mistral|dashscope|local] [--name f]
  artifact media tts "<text>" [--voice gb_oliver_neutral] [--name f]
  artifact media stt <audio-file>
  artifact media video "<prompt>" [--provider local|gemini]   (local: free, 2 s WebP, 10-20 min;
                                     gemini: METERED, only when the user asked for it)
  artifact media voices | capabilities

MOTION (animated explainers as code -> MP4; skill: dsh-motion)
  artifact motion check <name>       lint + runtime + layout + contrast gate (fix errors before export)
  artifact motion snapshot <name> [--at 1,4.5] [--frames 5]   PNG stills -> read them with read_image
  artifact motion export <name> [--quality draft|looks|delivery] [--format mp4|webm|gif|mov]
                     [--fps 30] [--resolution 4k] [--host auto|local|REMOTE]
                                     render; the player page shows the result (alias: artifact export)
  artifact motion voice <name> "<text>" [--voice v] [--id vo1] [--at 0]   TTS into assets/ + <audio> snippet

REFERENCE
  artifact help md       Markdown components (kpi, chart, form, actions, mermaid, ...)
  artifact help bridge   window.dsh API for hand-written pages and apps
  artifact libs          local libraries under /report/_lib (React, Tailwind, Chart.js, d3, three...)
"""
